        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Howard University Hospital, Freedmen's Hospital, Providence Hospital, The New Freedmen's Clinic, Howard University College of Medicine\n- Places: Washington, D.C., District of Columbia, Griffith Stadium\n- Topics: hospitals, free clinics, affiliations\n\nFacts:\n- Howard University Hospital, previously known as Freedmen's Hospital, is a major hospital in Washington, D.C., built on the site of the former Griffith Stadium.\n- The New Freedmen's Clinic first opened in the summer of 2009.\n- The New Freedmen's Clinic is a free student-run health care clinic affiliated with Howard University Hospital and Howard University College of Medicine.\n- Providence Hospital is a 408-bed hospital located in the District of Columbia.",
